<title>NETHERLANDS: AEGON Q1 NET RISES 24 PCT.</title>
<headline>AEGON Q1 NET RISES 24 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>THE HAGUE 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>First quarter 1997</p>
<p>(in millions of guilders unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Net per share (guilders)	  1.52 vs    1.24</p>
<p>    Net profit			  403.4  vs  325.6</p>
<p>    Turnover (billions)		 7.59 vs    6.70</p>
<p>Note: Dutch insurer Aegon NV was expected by analysts to</p>
<p>announce a net profit of between 363.5 million and 405 million</p>
<p>guilders.</p>
<p>    Tax				   115.0  vs   93.0</p>
<p>Breakdown of pre-tax profit:</p>
<p>    - Life insurance		  462    vs  368</p>
<p>    - Accident and health	    46    vs   35</p>
<p>    - General insurance		31    vs   23</p>
<p>    - Banking activities	     43    vs   35</p>
<p>    - Interest charges&amp;other  loss 64    vs   42 loss</p>
<p>Breakdown of revenue by sector:</p>
<p>    - Life insurance (billions)     4.23 vs    3.77</p>
<p>    - Accident and health	   703    vs  556</p>
<p>    - General insurance	     548    vs  499</p>
<p>    - Investment income (blns)	1.78 vs    1.58</p>
<p>    - Income from banking	   333    vs  296</p>
<p>    Benefits paid, provided (blns)  4.94 vs    4.46</p>
<p>    Commissions and expenses	980    vs  801</p>
<p>    Shareholders equity (blns)     12.74 vs   11.26</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
</text>
